.TH DFW 8 "November 2026" "dfw 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
dfw \- firewall for the containers on chosen Docker networks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dfw
.RB { plan " [" \fIFILE\fP "] | " apply | enable | disable | init " [" \-\-live "] | " run | active | version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dfw
filters the traffic of the containers on the Docker bridge networks named in
the rules, in an nftables table
.RB ( "bridge fw" )
on the ports of their bridges. The rules file names the networks and
lists the allowed connections; a container on them that no rule
mentions has no network access. Other networks are left alone. See
/usr/share/doc/dfw/README.md for the syntax.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR plan " [" \fIFILE\fP ]
Show the errors in the rules, what each running container on the filtered
networks would get, and their ports with no container behind them. With
.IR FILE ,
read the rules from that file alone, to check it before installing it.
Changes nothing. Exits 1 if the rules have errors.
.TP
.B apply
Apply the edited rules to the running dfw and wait until it confirms. Refuses
if the rules have errors, changing nothing. On a running system, editing the
rules has no effect until
.BR apply .
.TP
.B enable
Cut over: load the base table and every container's rules in one transaction,
cut the containers' tracked connections, write the docker.service drop-in and
start dfw.service. Refuses if the rules have errors. If dfw is already
running, the same as
.BR apply .
.TP
.B disable
Stop dfw.service, remove the drop-in and delete the table. This is the only
command that opens containers.
.TP
.BR init " [" \-\-live ]
Load the base table if it is missing or damaged; run by docker.service
before Docker starts. With
.BR \-\-live ,
also load every running container's rules in the same transaction.
.TP
.B run
Keep the table in line with the rules and Docker, and repair the table if
anything else changes it; run by dfw.service. At start it applies the rules
in /etc/dfw if they are valid, else the rules last applied; after that it
reloads them only through
.BR apply .
.TP
.B active
Exit 0 if dfw is enabled or its table is loaded.
.SH FILES
.TP
/etc/dfw/rules, /etc/dfw/rules.d/*.rules
The rules. Read in that order, as one file.
.TP
/var/lib/dfw/rules.json
The rules last applied.
.TP
/var/lib/dfw/open-bridges
The bridges to leave open at boot, before Docker can be asked.
.TP
/etc/systemd/system/docker.service.d/dfw.conf
Drop-in written by
.BR "dfw enable" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nft (8),
.BR conntrack (8)
